NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/server.Server.handleHalt kind=method
  digest=b3:5a035568f77e3844b8954244f7f18d9955fdc59e11eaa3ed1a031120ad119d84 file=neo/internal/server/server.go range=465:478 lang=go exported=false byte_range=20566:21290
  sig=func (s *Server) handleHalt(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
  doc=handleHalt is the global kill switch (POST /halt): it interrupts EVERY live\nNeo run this daemon is driving and reports how many were signalled. Each\ndaemon is single-tenant, so this stops exactly the calling user's own runaway\n/ parallel Neos — the deliberate "Stop all" escape hatch when the model is\nslow or a storm of respawns is underway. Idempotent: halting with nothing\nlive returns halted:0.
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/server.Server
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/server/server.go

